# Copy to .env.local for local development (never commit it).
# These two are PUBLIC values. Vite copies them into the website AT BUILD TIME, so on Cloudflare
# you must set them in the project's BUILD variables and then run a NEW deployment.
#   - no quote marks, no spaces, no trailing path
#   - the URL ends in  .supabase.co  (not .com)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://yjhtepcxpdoroptdrqoh.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_PASTE_YOUR_PUBLISHABLE_KEY_HERE
# (VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY is also accepted as an alternative name for the key.)
# The build STOPS with a clear message if these are wrong (scripts/check-env.mjs).

# ---- SERVER-SIDE SECRETS: never put these in a VITE_* variable, in git, or in chat. ----
# Set with:  supabase secrets set NAME=value   (run on your own machine, or Dashboard > Edge Functions > Secrets)
#   FLW_SECRET_KEY            Flutterwave secret key (TEST key only until launch sign-off)
#   FLW_WEBHOOK_SECRET_HASH   long random string; paste the SAME value in the Flutterwave dashboard
#   APP_URL                   exact public URL of the site, e.g. https://dream-game.pages.dev/
# SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected into Edge Functions automatically.
# NEVER put the Supabase "secret" / service_role key in the website or in Cloudflare build variables.
